<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liao River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> River is the main river of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a> in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, flowing about 1,345 km to the Bohai Sea. The grasslands of its upper basin were the homeland of the Khitan, whose Liao dynasty took its name from the river. Its lower valley, divided into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaodong">Liaodong</a> and Liaoxi, was long contested between Chinese states, Goguryeo and steppe powers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liao-river.jpg" alt="Liao River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 吴张帆 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E7%9B%98%E9%94%A6%E8%8A%A6%E8%8B%87%E8%8D%A1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
